## 7. System Architecture

The Smart Bus Reservation System follows a three-tier architecture consisting of the presentation layer, application layer and database layer.

### 7.1 Presentation Layer

The presentation layer represents the frontend of the application. It is developed using React.js, HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

It allows users to interact with the application through registration forms, login pages and reservation interfaces.

### 7.2 Application Layer

The application layer represents the backend functionality. It is developed using Java and Servlets.

Its responsibilities include:

- Processing user requests.
- Validating user information.
- Performing authentication operations.
- Communicating with the database.
- Returning responses to the frontend.

### 7.3 Database Layer

The database layer uses MySQL to store and manage application information.

It is responsible for:

- Storing user details.
- Retrieving registered user information.
- Maintaining reservation records.
- Supporting database operations.

