## 12. Database Management

MySQL is used as the database management system for the project.

The database provides a structured way to store and manage information.

Possible database tables include:

**Users Table**

Stores user registration and account information.

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| user_id | Unique user identification |
| name | User's full name |
| email | User's email address |
| password | Hashed password |
| created_at | Account creation date |

**Buses Table**

Stores information about available buses.

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| bus_id | Unique bus identification |
| bus_name | Name of the bus |
| source | Starting location |
| destination | Destination location |
| departure_time | Departure time |
| arrival_time | Arrival time |
| fare | Ticket price |

**Bookings Table**

Stores information about passenger reservations.

| Field | Description |
|---|---|
| booking_id | Unique booking identification |
| user_id | Registered user identification |
| bus_id | Selected bus identification |
| journey_date | Date of journey |
| seat_number | Selected seat |
| booking_status | Reservation status |

